# Reviewed test fixtures, path-and-rule form (file:rule:line). GYST v1.31.0 defaults the gitleaks scope to
# pr-commits, and a tree scan can only match this form, never the commit-bound one (commit:file:rule:line); a rebase
# or squash also orphans a commit id (GYST#336, #367). Each is a fake string; none is a credential.

# tests/test_mask.py: a fake PEM header (no key body); tests/test_action.py: two 40-hex action pins (public commit ids).
# Later commits build or no longer carry them as literals.
tests/test_mask.py:private-key:15
tests/test_action.py:generic-api-key:144
tests/test_action.py:generic-api-key:145

# tests/test_doctor.py: a fake token-shaped marker planted to prove it is never printed (#197). Later commits build
# it from plain words at run time. Two commit ids (before and after a rebase) collapse to this one entry.
tests/test_doctor.py:generic-api-key:23

# tests/test_broker_client.py (phase 4b client, feat/260-broker-client): a key-shaped string in a test. The owning PR
# builds it at run time; the old commit stays reachable. Can go when that branch is squash-merged.
tests/test_broker_client.py:generic-api-key:228

# tests/test_gemini_preflight.py (enrollment preflight, feat/263-enrollment-prep): a base64 public-key blob built
# from bytes 0..31 in a fake runner. Can go when that branch is squash-merged.
tests/test_gemini_preflight.py:generic-api-key:22
